# AddressSanitizer suppressions for the bug-hunting configuration.
#
# All entries here are third-party, not ours. Keep them as narrow as possible:
# each one is justified in TESTING.md and the final report.

# GoogleTest's JSON result printer (gtest.cc). CMake's gtest_discover_tests()
# runs the test binary with `--gtest_list_tests --gtest_output=json:...` at
# build time to enumerate the suite. libc++'s vector<string> range constructor
# over-allocates (the capacity is rounded up past the written size), and ASan's
# container-overflow check (only on in this configuration) reports a write into
# that slack while the printer copies label strings. It is a false positive:
# every element written is within size(), the JSON that comes out is valid and
# complete, and no frame of ours is involved. The suppressions file is only
# consulted during discovery and during ctest runs; nothing in our code paths
# reaches OutputJsonKey.
interceptor_via_fun:OutputJsonKey
